=== PARITY (vs web ChargeHistoryWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources → bound via the shared state-holder seam (ChargeHistorySource →
    ChargeHistoryModel): useVehicles (scoped id), useTranslation('dashboard'), useQuery
    (['charging', id, 'recent-10'] → GET /charging?vehicle_id=&limit=10). The production app
    wires the source over the KMP charging/vehicle stores; the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection → ChargeHistoryBuilder is a 1:1 port of the web `chartData` + `stats` memos:
    • map each session → kWh via convertEnergyFromSI(wh,'kWh') == wh/1000 (converter seam),
      keyed by the pre-reverse ordinal `i: String(index)` (preserved as axisLabel).
    • `.reverse()` so oldest is leftmost; stable zero-padded plotKey for ordering.
    • Total = Σenergy, Avg = total/len (fmt(_,1)); energyUnit fixed "kWh".
    • hasData == web `chartData.length > 1` (≥2 sessions; 1 or 0 → empty state).
  Layout → isCompact == web `size.cols <= 1` (column-only). Compact = stat row only (no chart),
    matching WidgetChartSummary compact; standard = stat row + AreaChart. Glass WidgetShell
    parity: title "Charge History" + BarChart3-equivalent green icon, freshness chip, refresh.
  Chart → web Recharts AreaChart (#10b981 monotone gradient, h=200, y=`${v} kWh`) →
    SwiftUI Charts AreaMark+LineMark with Color.TS.statusSuccess (== #10b981) gradient,
    monotone interpolation, tap-to-inspect RuleMark tooltip, thinned x-ticks on narrow widths.
  i18n → table "ChargeHistoryWidget"; all 5 web source strings present + verified:
    widget.chargeHistory.title/total/avg, widget.noChargeHistory, widget.chargeHistory.description.
  Registry → id "charge-history", category "charging", default 2×4, min 2×2, max 4×40 — unit-tested.

=== STATES (every state renders; no hidden surfaces) ===
  loading  → skeleton chrome (stat skeletons + chart skeleton)         [ChargeHistoryModel.Phase.loading]
  empty    → ContentUnavailableView "No charge sessions yet" + hint    [≤1 session OR none; web hasData>1]
  error    → icon + title + message + Retry affordance                 [.failed w/o cached points]
  stale    → amber banner + auto-refresh after 30s grace               [connection .stale]
  offline  → muted "showing last saved sessions" banner + cached chart [connection .offline]
  content  → stat row (Total/Avg kWh) + gradient area chart            [≥2 sessions]
  Cached points stay visible behind refresh/offline/error so a transient failure never blanks
  a populated widget (web shell keeps the last chartData).

